Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 09:43:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03061/11362] [outer-loop] LOCAL SUBMISSION GATE: refuse
 submits that locally regress (operator directive)

Never waste a 1/day Kaggle slot on a regression. scripts/kaggle/arc_local_submission_gate.py measures
the CURRENT submitted-default config (make_carnot_agent -> E3AgentPolicy, frame-only) on 8 fixed games
and compares to the verified baseline (ops/arc-submission-baseline.json) on the two scoring-relevant
metrics: solve-rate AND action efficiency (median actions/solve -- score is (human/agent)^2). PASS only
if NON-INFERIOR on both. Wired into prep_daily_submission.py:submit_only -> refuses unless --force.
Baseline seeded from the verified bare-BFS measurement (4 solved, median 2931 actions). VERIFIED: the
current regressed E3+v3 config FAILS the gate (1 solved vs 4, median 7792 vs 2931) -> exit 1 -> submit
blocked. Update the baseline only on a confirmed leaderboard improvement (--update-baseline).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
